.TH WLPIPES 1 "2026-09-25" "wlpipes 0.4.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wlpipes \- Windows XP 3D Pipes recreation for Wayland
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wlpipes
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A native animation client with per-output scenes and shared process random state.
Normal single/multiple growth, all joint and surface modes, layout and timing are
reconstructed from XP's executable. Materials use per-vertex Gouraud lighting.
Original artwork is not bundled; some texture-wrap behavior is driver-dependent. Runtime/pixel equivalence is not yet verified.
This is NOT a screen locker. Use swaylock-plugin for separate authentication.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-windowed
Use an ordinary xdg-shell preview window.
.TP
.B \-\-overlay
Fullscreen layer-shell overlay (default), dismissed by input when used standalone.
.TP
.BI \-\-pipes " MODE"
single (default), multiple, or an exact count from 1 to 4. Multiple randomly
chooses 2..4 heads per scene; numeric counts fix the initial head count each scene.
Counts above one default to seven starts per solid scene (four when textured) and the
reference's persistent chase behavior.
.TP
.BI \-\-joints " MODE"
Elbow (default), ball, mixed or cycle. Mixed chooses a ball on one of three random
buckets at each turn. Cycle advances Elbow/Ball/Mixed at scene resets.
.TP
.BI \-\-texture " PATH"
Select a BMP/JPEG/TGA/PNG custom texture.
.TP
.BI \-\-default-texture " PATH"
Select a locally supplied default bitmap, also used if the custom texture fails.
No texture arguments means Solid. Requested assets must exist and pass limits.
.TP
.BI \-\-tessellation " N"
XP mesh quality, 0..4. Default 0; slice counts are 8, 12, 20, 28 and 36.
.TP
.BI \-\-speed-level " N"
XP speed slider, 0..20. Default 16 has a strict 20 ms render-eligibility gate.
20 removes that software gate but remains callback-paced. There is no catch-up.
The old millisecond speed option is rejected, not silently reinterpreted.
.TP
.BI \-\-scene-length " N"
Multiply the scene's pipe-start budget by 1..10 (default 1), allowing more growth
before fading without changing speed or head count. A full grid can end a scene
earlier; this is not an exact duration multiplier.
.TP
.BI \-\-seed " N"
Unsigned 32-bit XP RNG state before ten warm-up draws. Default startup seed is
the wall clock's millisecond field. RNG parity alone is not whole-scene parity.
.TP
.BI \-\-max-seconds " N"
Exit after 1..86400 seconds, even without frame callbacks.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage without opening a display.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show version.
.SH LAYOUT
XP layout always derives from each output's aspect ratio: 15 nodes along the
longer axis and depth 15. Geometry is not stretched to fill a modern fitted box.
The old grid, continuous-rotate, teapot, max-runs and max-length options have
been removed. Normal single scenes allow five solid or three textured starts and
grow until trapped. Texture repetition uses target pixels, not a fixed UV scale.
.SH LIMITS
The aggregate model/command/upload budget is 128 MiB; retained colour/depth targets
share a separate 512-MiB padded-storage budget with owned mesh and texture data.
Driver window buffers are additional. Buffers are capped at 16384 per dimension, 64 megapixels and actual GL
capabilities. Rebuild replay is bounded at 4096 accumulated fade passes.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0: dismissal, timeout, help or version. 1: runtime failure. 2: invalid arguments.
.SH AUTHORS
The native Wayland port originated in flacyak/wlpipes. Retained code is attributed
in LICENSE and NOTICE. No Microsoft program or artwork is included.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR swaylock-plugin (1)
